course: dictionary
lesson: 2527
title: Decoration
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A decoration is something added to make a thing or place look pretty or special. Context often gives you the meaning. «Many holidays have traditions — things people do the same way every year, like special food, songs or decorations.» Food and songs are things we do to celebrate, so decorations must be things that make a celebration look special.
explain: The sentence «Decorator crabs stick bits of sponge and seaweed on their shells to hide» tells you more. Bits of sponge and seaweed are stuck on the shell, so decorations can be things stuck onto something else. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence? Balloons on a wall fit, and so does tinsel on a tree.
explain: Decoration can also mean the act of decorating, as in the decoration of a room. Another meaning is a medal given as an honour. Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: A decoration is something added to make a thing or place look pretty or special.
fact: Balloons, tinsel and ornaments are all decorations.
fact: Decoration can also mean the act of decorating, like putting up or taking down the decorations for a party.
fact: «Decorations away from candles and fires» is a safety rule, because decorations can catch fire.
fact: A decoration can also be a medal given as an honour.
exercise: Decorator crabs stick bits of sponge and seaweed on their shells. What are the bits of sponge and seaweed? | Food the crabs eat | Tools for digging | Their homes | *Decorations, things stuck on to look different
exercise: Which of these is a decoration for a birthday party? | *Balloons | A bag of rice | Shoes | Homework
exercise: «Keep decorations away from candles and fires.» Why is this a safety rule? | *Candles and fires could set the decorations alight | So they can fly | To make them dry | To make the room darker
test: Which of these is not a decoration? | Paper chains | Tinsel | *A spoon for stirring soup | Ornaments
test: A soldier is given a decoration for bravery. What is the decoration? | A uniform | A kind of paint | A cake | *A medal given as an honour
exam: Which sentence uses decoration to mean the act of decorating? | *We spent all afternoon on the decoration of the hall. | He was given a decoration for courage. | The decoration was a silver star on top of the tree. | Decorations should be kept away from heat.
